  "problem": {
    "id": "train-4932",
    "question": "A movie theater charges $5 for matinee tickets, $7 for evening tickets, and $10 for opening night tickets. A bucket of popcorn costs $10. On Friday, they had 32 matinee customers, 40 evening customers, and 58 customers for an opening night showing of a movie. If half the customers bought popcorn, how much money in dollars did the theater make on Friday night?",
    "gold": "1670",
    "answer": "The movie theater made 5 * 32 = $<<5*32=160>>160 in matinee tickets.\nIt made 7 * 40 = $<<7*40=280>>280 in evening tickets.\nIt made 10 * 58 = $<<10*58=580>>580 in opening night tickets.\nThere were 32 + 40 + 58 = <<32+40+58=130>>130 customers.\nHalf of the customers bought popcorn, so 130 / 2 = <<130/2=65>>65 bought popcorn.\nThus, the theater made 10 * 65 = $<<10*65=650>>650 from popcorn.\nTherefore, in all, the theater made 160 + 280 + 580 + 650 = $<<160+280+580+650=1670>>1670 on Friday night.\n#### 1670"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much money the theater made on Friday night, we need to calculate the revenue from ticket sales and popcorn sales separately, and then sum these amounts.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the revenue from ticket sales:\n- The number of matinee customers is 32, and each matinee ticket costs $5. So, the revenue from matinee tickets is:\n  \\[\n  32 \\times 5 = 160 \\text{ dollars}\n  \\]\n- The number of evening customers is 40, and each evening ticket costs $7. So, the revenue from evening tickets is:\n  \\[\n  40 \\times 7 = 280 \\text{ dollars}\n  \\]\n- The number of opening night customers is 58, and each opening night ticket costs $10. So, the revenue from opening night tickets is:\n  \\[\n  58 \\times 10 = 580 \\text{ dollars}\n  \\]\nAdding these amounts together gives the total revenue from ticket sales:\n\\[\n160 + 280 + 580 = 920 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the revenue from popcorn sales:\n- Half of the customers bought popcorn, so the number of customers who bought popcorn is:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{32 + 40 + 58}{2} = \\frac{130}{2} = 65\n  \\]\n- Each bucket of popcorn costs $10, so the revenue from popcorn sales is:\n  \\[\n  65 \\times 10 = 650 \\text{ dollars}\n  \\]\n\nFinally, we add the revenue from ticket sales and popcorn sales to get the total revenue for the night:\n\\[\n920 + 650 = 1570 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nThus, the total amount of money the theater made on Friday night is \\(\\boxed{1570}\\).",
